DATA.writing = [
{ id: "w1", part: 1, title: "Joining a book club", min: 5, max: 25,
  prompt: "You are joining a book club. Answer each message with 1–5 words.\n1. What's your name?\n2. What kind of books do you like?\n3. When do you usually read?\n4. How many books do you read a year?\n5. Where do you buy your books?",
  model: "1. Alex García\n2. Crime novels\n3. Before going to bed\n4. About ten\n5. In a second-hand bookshop",
  tips: ["Short answers are fine here. No full sentences needed.", "Check spelling and capital letters. That's what is marked."] },
{ id: "w2", part: 2, title: "New member form", min: 20, max: 30,
  prompt: "You are a new member of a sports club. Fill in the form. Write in sentences. Use 20–30 words.\n\"Please tell us why you are interested in sport.\"",
  model: "I have always enjoyed sport because it keeps me fit and helps me relax after work. I am especially keen on swimming and would love to try tennis.",
  tips: ["Write full sentences with correct punctuation.", "Useful: I'm keen on… / I'm interested in + -ing / because it helps me…"] },
{ id: "w3", part: 3, title: "Travel club chat", min: 90, max: 120,
  prompt: "You are a member of a travel club and you are chatting to Sam in the club chat room. Answer each question with 30–40 words.\nSam: Hi! Welcome to the club. Why did you join?\nSam: What's the most interesting place you have visited?\nSam: We're planning a weekend trip. Where do you think we should go, and why?",
  model: "1. I joined because I love discovering new places but I'm tired of travelling on my own. I'm hoping to meet people who enjoy the same things and to get some ideas for future trips.\n\n2. Probably Edinburgh. I went there two years ago and was amazed by the castle and the old streets. The weather was awful, but the people were so friendly that I didn't mind at all.\n\n3. How about the Lake District? It isn't too far, the scenery is breathtaking and there are walks for every level. We could stay in a hostel, which would keep the cost down.",
  tips: ["Friendly, natural style: contractions are fine (I'm, didn't).", "Answer all three questions and stay on topic.", "Useful: How about…? / We could… / I was amazed by…"] },
{ id: "w4", part: 4, title: "Informal email: trip cancelled", min: 40, max: 50,
  prompt: "You are a member of a travel club. You received this notice:\n\"Dear member, we are sorry to tell you that the trip to Bath next Saturday has been cancelled because not enough people booked. Fees will not be refunded, but they may be used for a future trip.\"\nWrite an email to a friend who is also a member. Say how you feel and what you plan to do. Write 40–50 words.",
  model: "Hi Laura,\nHave you seen the notice about the Bath trip? I can't believe they've cancelled it! I was looking forward to it, and it's so unfair that we won't get our money back. I'm going to complain to the secretary. Fancy going on our own instead?\nSpeak soon,\nAlex",
  tips: ["Informal register: Hi…, contractions, exclamation marks, phrasal verbs.", "Useful: I can't believe… / Fancy + -ing? / Speak soon"] },
{ id: "w5", part: 4, title: "Formal email: trip cancelled", min: 120, max: 150,
  prompt: "You are a member of a travel club. You received this notice:\n\"Dear member, we are sorry to tell you that the trip to Bath next Saturday has been cancelled because not enough people booked. Fees will not be refunded, but they may be used for a future trip.\"\nWrite an email to the secretary of the club. Explain how you feel and suggest alternatives. Write 120–150 words.",
  model: "Dear Sir or Madam,\n\nI am writing with regard to the notice I received about the cancellation of next Saturday's trip to Bath.\n\nI must say that I am extremely disappointed. I have been a member of the club for three years and I booked this trip several months ago. In addition, I find it unacceptable that the fees will not be refunded, since the decision to cancel was taken by the club and not by the members.\n\nI would like to suggest two alternatives. Firstly, the trip could be postponed rather than cancelled, which would give more people the chance to book. Secondly, members who are unable to attend on a new date should be offered a full refund.\n\nI would be grateful if you could let me know your decision as soon as possible.\n\nI look forward to hearing from you.\n\nYours faithfully,\nAlex García",
  tips: ["Formal register: no contractions, no exclamation marks.", "Dear Sir or Madam → Yours faithfully. Dear Mr Smith → Yours sincerely.", "Useful: I am writing with regard to… / I would like to suggest… / I would be grateful if you could…"] },
{ id: "w6", part: 4, title: "Formal email: the library", min: 120, max: 150,
  prompt: "You live in a small town. You read this notice:\n\"The council has decided to close the town library at the end of the year in order to save money. Residents may send their comments to the council.\"\nWrite an email to the council. Explain how you feel about the decision and suggest other ways of solving the problem. Write 120–150 words.",
  model: "Dear Sir or Madam,\n\nI am writing to express my concern about the council's decision to close the town library at the end of the year.\n\nAlthough I understand that the council needs to save money, I strongly believe that this would be a serious mistake. The library is not only a place to borrow books; it is also where students revise, where elderly residents meet and where people without a computer can go online. If it closed, many of them would have nowhere else to go.\n\nI would like to suggest some alternatives. The library could reduce its opening hours instead of closing completely. Furthermore, local volunteers might be willing to help the staff, and the building could be hired out for events in the evenings to raise money.\n\nI hope you will reconsider your decision.\n\nYours faithfully,\nAlex García",
  tips: ["Structure: reason for writing → how you feel → suggestions → closing line.", "Show range: although, furthermore, a second conditional (If it closed, … would…).", "Useful: I am writing to express my concern about… / I strongly believe that…"] }
];

